A||||7||MinnGreenGT||Squeaky Body Panels...?||||1||
Z||000000||MinnGreenGT||07-30-2001||04:29 PM||||I have an '87 GT with a handful of modifications-none of which really have anything to do with the problem.  My roof "Squeaks" when I drive. At first I thought It may be the windows- but I can stop the squeaking (or "Chirping") by pressing down on top of the panel while driving.  Is there any specific suggested way to stop this- there are also a few squeaks in the interior. I had someone mention using silicon and basically re-caulking under the panel? Does that sound feasible? Same for the interior...  any help or advice would be great!<P>Thanks in advance!<BR>Rob Bartlett<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngt.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||07-30-2001||06:46 PM||||take out the headliner and tighten all the nuts.<P>unless you mean a sunroof. then you need some adjustments and maybe some new parts for the thing.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 07-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||07-31-2001||09:28 AM||||Actually the interior isn't too bad.  Primarily the noise is actually coming from the exterior roof panel.||||reg||1
Z||000003||KRMFiero||07-31-2001||10:14 AM||||He means take the headliner out and there will be serveral bolts holding on the roof skin, tightin them and it might stop the squeeking<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||07-31-2001||10:30 AM||||The nuts have a soft molded rubber behind them.  Over time it wears thin.  Tightening them just a bit should probably do the trick. <P>I replaced mine some thin neoprene washers from the hardware store because the rubber backings were crumbling apart.  Worked great.||||reg||1
